35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The technicians are gone, but the glasshouse crew remains. We have the hands, yet the minds are abroad.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Thank you, Servas. My findings show computing is free, but animal-unit day rates spiked. Travel costs are frozen, yet shipping climbed.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, the spectroscopy suite was idle for eleven weeks! That’s scary. One engineer for three institutes? We really need to check if that’s fixed.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Kenji, that idle suite is a red flag. My data shows biology-heavy projects stall twice as often. We must prioritize candidates with robust, non-biological workflows.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The closeout files confirm my suspicion. Catalogue awards persist; mechanism-focused ones stall. We should value sustained utility over initial promise.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Toshio, your insight is profound. We must value the hands that remain. The glasshouse crew is our true foundation, not the absent minds.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"I hear you, Servas. But if animal costs spike, even the best hands struggle. We must balance the budget with the staffing reality.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I agree! If the spectroscopy suite is broken, biology projects are at risk. We should pick candidates who don’t rely on that specific equipment.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, precisely. We cannot gamble on a single engineer’s availability. Let’s favor proposals with computational depth over those dependent on fragile, shared biological infrastructure.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,I note the repository turnaround improved. That removes a logistical bottleneck. We can now focus purely on the scientific merit and long-term utility of the candidates.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"Midori, your caution is vital. We must ensure the budget supports the crew that actually remains, not the ghosts of departed technicians.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"Thank you, Servas. I agree. We must ensure the budget supports the crew that actually remains, not the ghosts of departed technicians.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,I’m glad the animal facility is safe! But that idle spectroscopy suite worries me. Let’s hope the new engineer can keep up with the demand.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Kenji, hope is not a strategy. We need candidates whose timelines survive the current staffing reality, not just good intentions.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
